+`setEditorComponent` is wired to the live editor (`ctx.setEditorComponent(factory)`). `setWidget` renders real widget components via `setHookWidget(...)`: `placement: "aboveEditor"` (default), `"belowEditor"` (before the native status footer), or `"belowFooter"` (after the native status footer). String-array content is capped at 10 lines. Moving or clearing a widget key removes its previous placement. `setEditorText` and `pasteToEditor` schedule a repaint after mutating the editor, so prompt changes don't leave stale content on screen.
+
+Interactive widgets can inspect `ctx.ui.getNativeFooter(width)` for the current native footer without widget content. A `belowFooter` component may expose `footerColumnWidths: readonly number[]` to request minimum native column widths. Requests are combined across widgets and use only spare space after native overflow handling; they do not change saved settings or remove native fields. Clearing or moving the widgets releases their width requests.
 
